{"id": "EUVD-2026-101233", "enisaUuid": "68ebfc33-333b-3f48-9d71-a9d503027945", "description": "libschrift through 0.10.2 contains a divide by zero vulnerability that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying a font with unitsPerEm of 0 in the head table. Attackers can provide a crafted TrueType font whose NaN glyph coordinates bypass clip_points(), causing an out-of-bounds raster read in draw_line() during sft_render() and crashing the process.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T14:16:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T14:16:45", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/tomolt/libschrift/issues/46", "https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libschrift-unitsperem-zero-oob", "https://github.com/tomolt/libschrift/blob/v0.10.2/schrift.c#L542", "https://github.com/tomolt/libschrift/blob/v0.10.2/schrift.c#L1422-L1503", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libschrift-through-0.10.2-divide-by-zero-via-unitsperem-in-draw-line"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110605", "GHSA-h8w2-cf8p-7p38"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "cf0061a0-6353-36b7-9323-b84685459dcd", "product": {"name": "libschrift", "vendor": {"name": "tomolt"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.10.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cccdd6db-f259-35e7-aade-5a74fec9283a", "vendor": {"name": "tomolt"}}], "isExploited": false}